<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>PDF Note – Rust crate licenses</title>
<style>
  body { font: 14px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 960px; margin: 2em auto; padding: 0 1em; }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1em; }
  .used-by { columns: 3; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>PDF Note – Rust crate licenses</h1>
<p>Licenses of all Rust crates compiled into PDF Note (target x86_64-pc-windows-msvc), generated with cargo-about from Cargo.lock.
The source code of every crate listed here is available unchanged on https://crates.io (version as listed); this also covers the
source-availability notice of the Mozilla Public License 2.0. The crate <code>mupdf</code> is patched, see vendor/mupdf/PATCH.md in the
PDF Note source code.</p>
<h2>Overview</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}  <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}</ul>
<h2>License texts</h2>
{{#each licenses}}<section>
<h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>
<p>Used by:</p>
<ul class="used-by">
{{#each used_by}}  <li>{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</li>
{{/each}}</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
</section>
{{/each}}</body>
</html>
